# x86_64 baseline of the final hardening build.
# Measured locally with scripts/check-sizes.sh on the reference desktop,
# built from commit 70e9984 (tree clean apart from documentation), rustc
# 1.98.1 from rust-toolchain.toml, release profile (fat LTO,
# codegen-units=1, panic=abort, strip). The sources of the shipped
# binaries changed since the previous baseline (420a714) by the second
# buffer's first-touch move, the Undo/Trash ownership rule and the
# measurement markers.
# The per-area account of the growth over the Plan 7 baseline
# (inacircle 900352 671864) is in docs/benchmarks/binary-size.md.
# Refreshed after the pages-to-PDF work on this x86_64 desktop, built from
# commit 8cf5df2 (tree clean), same toolchain and profile: inacircle grew
# 1112 B (file) and the pages family 3224 B; the shipped inacircle does not
# link the new zip, flate, probe or pdf crates.
# Refreshed after the many-inputs-to-one-output work on this x86_64 desktop,
# built from commit 9f808bcd (tree clean), same toolchain and profile: inacircle
# grew 40472 B (file) and the pages family 13352 B (file, 12432 B of .text), both under the
# 100 KB explanation threshold; the shipped inacircle still does not link
# the zip, flate, probe or pdf crates.
# Refreshed after the wheel drop-list and memory work (list limit, paths held
# once, owned uri-list parser), same toolchain and profile: inacircle grew
# 3592 B (file, 3024 B of .text); the other two binaries are unchanged.
inacircle 1150712 883336
inacircle-text 695000 397314
inacircle-pages 464592 372211
